// S441 reproducer — addendum item 21: an inline `onsubmit=${ … }` handler gets no `event.preventDefault()`,
// so the browser natively submits and reloads; `onsubmit=fn()` on the same page gets it.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/inline-onsubmit-block-no-preventdefault.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: both forms behave the same. RULING-GATED on the SPEC side (no sentence mandates the auto-inject; see
//           the gap), but the compiler's own convention is auto-inject for submit (emit-event-wiring.ts:~1262).
// Actual:   exit 0. client.js submit registry:
//             "_scrml_attr_onsubmit_1": function(event) { event.preventDefault(); _scrml_go_5(); },
//             "_scrml_attr_onsubmit_3": function(event) { _scrml_cs_reactive_set("n", _scrml_cs_reactive_get("n") + 1); },
//           Form B reloads the page on submit; an async server call in the block (the onboarding login shape,
//           `onsubmit=${ @token = login(@email, @password) }`) is cut off by the navigation.
<program>
<q> = ""
<n> = 0
function go() { @n = @n + 1 }
<form onsubmit=go()>
    <input bind:value=@q/>
    <button type="submit">A</button>
</form>
<form onsubmit=${ @n = @n + 1 }>
    <button type="submit">B</button>
</form>
<p>${@n}</p>
</program>
